WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:06.310
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and my Game of
Thrones countdown continues, I think we’re

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.200
on our third or fourth video.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.309
During my Breakdown of the last trailer I
asked you all to submit questions and I picked

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:15.309
10 to answer with one bonus question.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:17.820
Everybody really just wants to talk about
the Titan of Braavos, but I grabbed some other

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:18.820
good ones.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.620
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m doing a special countdown series for

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.620
the Season 4 premiere.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.039
I’ve got a bunch of cool stuff planned so
subscribe to get everything.

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:29.009
I’m even doing a weekly giveaway once the
season starts.

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:30.920
Now it’s time to talk some Braavos.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.930
Careful for spoilers if you’re not caught
up on the show.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.420
Here we go.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:40.170
Question Number 1 - Neto del Toro asks Do
you think we’ll see Cat of The Canals House

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:44.280
of Black and White this season based on The
Titan being in the trailer?

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.860
Based on that Titan, yes we will see Braavos
but not quite the way you think.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.580
There’s a lot of different stories tied
up in that location during various parts of

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.790
the story, but the one I think we’ll see
is Ser Davos at the Iron Bank.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:00.670
Remember Mark Gatiss is playing Tycho Nestoris,
someone who works at the Iron Bank.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.809
Stannis had no money during season 2 when
he borrowed all those ships from Salladhor

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:05.869
Saan’s ships.

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:09.119
The funny thing about that scene was that
all that Saan seemed to want was to get to

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:12.100
have sex with Cersei when they took King’s
Landing.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:17.240
But since that very expensive fleet was torched
with wildfire, Stannis has no more ships and

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.240
no money.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.869
So Davos will get sent to borrow more.

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:22.520
Enter Mark Gatiss.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.570
Question 2 - Fenrirnorgesen asks when the
show catches up to the books will the do a

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.479
prequel series like for dunk and egg or Robert’s
Rebellion?

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:36.210
Yes there will be a prequel tv series at some
point, but it will be set way way back in

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.210
the past.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.920
So no Dunk and Egg and no Robert’s Rebellion.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.979
George RR Martin was signed to an HBO development
deal of his own around season 1.

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:49.939
I personally want to see a series set in Old
Valyria before the doom.

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:53.710
It’s the same situation with Robert Kirkman
at AMC.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.159
They also signed him to a development deal
for a Walking Dead spinoff show.

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:01.420
It’s just because those world’s are so
popular, and HBO and AMC want to keep that

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.829
type of content going for as long as possible.

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:08.130
No announcements have been made about the
Game of Thrones Prequel series, but it took

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:12.690
David Benioff and DB Weiss 3 years to make
the first pilot for the current Game of Thrones

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:13.690
show.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.480
Plus Martin still has to finish Winds of Winter
and then write Dream of Spring.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.420
He’s a busy man.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:24.450
Question 3 - Taylor Simpson asks will they
add scenes for characters that aren’t in

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.800
Feast For Crows or Dance With Dragons?

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.170
You’re talking about the same thing they
did with Theon last season.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:37.360
Yes, they’ll re-arrange things so that they
happen chronologically.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.580
It just makes it easier to follow a story
when you don’t jump back and forth in time

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.580
too much.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.880
JRR Tolkein had the same problem with his
books, so Peter Jackson had to re-arrange

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.710
the chapters for the movies so that events
unfolded one right after the other.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:55.440
As far as extra things, they’re really just
blending Feast for Crows with Dance with Dragons.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.450
They won’t cover all of those books, but
most of the characters that aren’t in Feast

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:04.290
are in Dance, so logically it made sense to
do events from the beginning of both books.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.540
A lot of the later chapters will probably
spill over into season 5 though.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:15.370
Question 4 - Vermalgab Boom asks Is anyone
going to go to Braavos since we saw the Titan?

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:21.590
Yes, Davos like I mentioned, but I also think
that we’ll see teasers at the end for other

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.560
characters that are going there.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:29.150
There’s at least two or four I guess, depending
on how you look at it.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:34.620
Question 5 - Sergio Vale da Serra asks, Do
you think Ned Stark will come back?

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.720
What do you think the cliffhanger will be
this season?

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:43.880
The only way Ned Stark could come back would
be as a Wight, and even then he’s lost his

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.600
head, so I don’t think the white walkers
would be able to re-animate his corpse.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.840
The only way to kill them is to burn the bodies,
so I guess they could reanimate his head so

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.930
that he’s just a biter like the ones in
the Governor’s fish tank on walking dead.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:59.890
As far as cliffhangers, there are several
events in the middle of books four and five

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.250
that would be good.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.810
All of the characters have multiple oh shit
moments, so it will be amazing no matter where

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.200
they end things.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:13.280
Question 6 - Steven U asks Will we finally
get to see Barristan Selmy fight this season?

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.200
I hope so, the show stays really close to
the spirit of the books and major plot points.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.109
But it does take small liberties with characters.

00:04:21.109 --> 00:04:24.949
As we’ve seen in the trailers, Daenerys
still has a major battle ahead of her and

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:28.530
while all the Barristan Selmy scenes make
him seem like more of a talker and less of

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.040
a stabber, I think he will get tough with
people.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.849
Daario is really the stabby one in her camp,
the one who gets sent out to quote unquote,

00:04:36.849 --> 00:04:38.150
take care of things.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.620
Selmy is really more of a counselor, like
Ser Friendzone.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.400
With way less creepiness about him.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.590
Question 7 - Conner Peckham (no avatar) asks
I kinda want to start on the books, but I

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.710
want to start reading where the show is right
now.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:50.840
Which book should I start with?

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.220
Honestly, you need to read the second half
of Storm of Swords if you really want to pick

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:57.189
up where Season 3 left off.

00:04:57.189 --> 00:05:01.789
But if you want to be quick about it, you
can just read spoilers for that stuff and

00:05:01.789 --> 00:05:03.740
start reading A Feast For Crows.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:08.240
Season 4 is going to be weird in that it combines
chapters from the first half of both Book

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.520
4 and 5.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.349
So you’ll miss out on some stuff no matter
what.

00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:15.069
But I think if you’re going to read the
books, you should read them in the order they

00:05:15.069 --> 00:05:18.169
were published, not in the order the show
is doing them.

00:05:18.169 --> 00:05:20.250
When the season does start and I do videos
for the episodes.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:23.539
I’ll try to reference chapters of events
when they happen on the show.

00:05:23.539 --> 00:05:25.800
In case anyone wants to compare.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.909
Question 8 - Lisa Cunningham asks How far
into the storyline of Cercei do you think

00:05:29.909 --> 00:05:31.419
they will get this season?

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:34.520
I think we’ll only get about halfway through
her character’s arc.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.949
So there will still be a lot of big stuff
spilling over into Season 5.

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:41.949
With all the mega stuff going on in King’s
Landing already, including everything from

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:45.469
her chapters seems like it would be too much
for the story to handle.

00:05:45.469 --> 00:05:49.620
The problem with the show is that if it tried
to do everything in a single book for a season

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.550
it would be way too disorganized.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:56.449
And remember, she’s not going to be in every
single episode.

00:05:56.449 --> 00:06:02.139
Question 9 - Ryuga Zero asks Who do you think
is the most important character or will become

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:03.939
the most important character?

00:06:03.939 --> 00:06:10.169
So this is a huge debate, but George RR Martin
has always said that he identifies with Tyrion

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.169
the most.

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:15.599
I always felt that a lot of fantasy authors
make some of the narrative autobiographical,

00:06:15.599 --> 00:06:20.279
in the sense that the character they identify
with the most becomes the most important character.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:24.400
That’s not always the case, but there’s
something really logical about the way David

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.360
Benioff and DB Weiss went about casting Peter
Dinklage.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.259
He’s the highest paid actor on the show.

00:06:29.259 --> 00:06:35.469
Yes, they are following the plot of the books
for the big stuff.

00:06:35.469 --> 00:06:40.590
The other clear choice is Daenerys, she’s
been the face of the show on the posters and

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.499
everything for a couple seasons now.

00:06:42.499 --> 00:06:47.680
The thing I really like about Game of Thrones
is that unlike say, The Hobbit or Lord of

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:48.680
The Rings.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.780
There is no one single main character.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:54.469
But if I had to pick it would be a tie between
Tyrion and Daenerys.

00:06:54.469 --> 00:06:59.930
Question 10 - Henri-Martin Fayad asks How
do you think the first episode will start?

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.530
Typically the first episode of each new season
of Game of Thrones has started immediately

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:06.629
after the events of the previous season’s
finale.

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:12.680
So if you re-watch the last episode of season
3, we’ll start season 4 a few days after

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.680
that.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:18.389
So Jon Snow just came back to the Night’s
Watch, Daenerys just freed all those slaves

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:20.999
and Jaime and Brienne just came back to King’s
Landing.

00:07:20.999 --> 00:07:24.180
So those will be the places we’ll start
with in episode 1.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:30.210
and one last Bonus Question - Ayan Tandon
asks how many seasons will there be?

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:38.319
The showrunners just did an interview with
Vanity Fair where they said they went to George

00:07:38.319 --> 00:07:42.770
RR Martin’s house in New Mexico to learn
how the rest of the story ends for each character.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.490
That’s just because by the time we get through
season 5, they’ll have passed the books.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:51.789
They didn’t reveal any spoilers of course,
but they did say they have enough content

00:07:51.789 --> 00:07:57.389
for 7 seasons and maybe an 8th, depending
if HBO would pay for it.

00:07:57.389 --> 00:08:00.150
Believe me, they will pay for an 8th season.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:04.960
For now, we can say confirmed 7, but in reality
I do think it will be 8.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:08.800
So thanks so much for submitting questions,
this was a lot of fun.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.850
I’m working on getting livestreaming running
on my channel.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:14.050
So I might do live Q&amp;A videos in the future.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:22.369
I’m also working on doing live videos right
after shows end, like Talking Dead.

00:08:22.369 --> 00:08:25.650
That probably won’t happen at least until
Game of Thrones starts.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:29.580
I have a lot of technical details to work
out.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:33.060
Be sure to subscribe to get the rest of my
countdown videos.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:38.769
My next video is going to be a history of
Dragons in the world of Essos.

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:42.610
Remember they started out in Valyria, then
came to Westeros and so on.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:45.259
That will probably post late late tonight.

00:08:45.259 --> 00:08:51.280
Right now click here to watch all my breakdown
videos and click here for my Walking Dead

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:55.390
predictions, because we only have 3 more episodes
this season.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.120
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:57.649
High Fives!

